  "3": {
    "citation": "(13)",
    "context": "Then, the total additive error of the standard CM sketch is computed as LCM=n\u2211\ufe02 j=1\u03b5A(ej)=n\u2211\ufe02 j=1N\u2212f(ej) w=nN w\u2212N w=(n\u22121)N w(13) Now, let us computeL FCM, the total additive error for the FCM sketch. LFCM=n\u2211\ufe02 j=1\u03b5A(ej)=\u2211\ufe02 ej\u2208g1\u03b5A(ej)+\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7+\u2211\ufe02 ej\u2208gl\u03b5A(ej) Following the same calculation as in Equation (13), for every groupg\u2208G, \u2211\ufe02 ej\u2208g\u03b5A(ej)=(n g\u22121)Ng wg Hence, LFCM=\u2211\ufe02 ej\u2208g1\u03b5A(ej)+\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7+\u2211\ufe02 ej\u2208gl\u03b5A(ej)=\u2211\ufe02 g\u2208G(ng\u22121)Ng wg From Theorem 1, we know,w g=ng nw,\u2200g\u2208G, while\u2211\ufe01 g\u2208GNg=N."
